  {
    "id": "core:interior/the_struck_barrow",
    "name": "The Struck Barrow",
    "scene": "res://world/sites/site_interior.tscn",
    "kind": "deep_place",
    "place": "core:poi/the_struck_barrow",
    "danger": 3,
    "formed_by": "builder",
    "resident": "four thousand struck debtors on numbered shelves, some of them up; a bailiff who never stopped distraining; resurrection men copying names to sell; and Obadiah Fenn, the last Receiver, at the register",
    "story": "The Tallymen cut the barrow like a counting-house: a receiving-room at the door with a bier for a table, a weighing-room where each body was set on the beam against its debt in lead, and shelves, level under level, numbered and never named. The Receiver entered every one in the Barrow Register and struck the name in the city's Roll the same day. When the post's fees fell owing in 1019 the Tallymen struck him too, and nobody came to receive the Receiver. He is still at the register at the bottom of the barrow, entering.",
    "unique_object": "the beam-scale in the weighing-room, its pans big enough for a man, a heap of lead debt-weights stamped with sums beside it, and the barrow's lime-washed shelves numbered in black to four thousand and eleven",
